                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or exhibiting equality in dimensions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "523d29ff-c7a7-388a-890c-598d9161d4b6",
                                        "entry_id": "cf9e2bdb-0efb-317e-a45a-b9c65bdd4b8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being or relating to a geometric system of three equal axes lying at right angles to each other (especially in crystallography)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57d054f1-bfd3-380a-a3a9-20a2c5abb404",
                                        "entry_id": "cf9e2bdb-0efb-317e-a45a-b9c65bdd4b8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or involving muscular contraction against resistance in which the length of the muscle remains the same. See also: Wikipedia:isometric exercise"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6308001-29da-4435-9e06-b10888f2a979",
                                                "sense_id": "57d054f1-bfd3-380a-a3a9-20a2c5abb404",
                                                "text": "One of the most effective isometric exercises for the deskbound is to sit up quite straight and tighten the large muscles of the buttocks, holding for a count of eight, then release."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46b86f08-f455-4642-91e9-3abef3e70bef",
                                                "sense_id": "57d054f1-bfd3-380a-a3a9-20a2c5abb404",
                                                "text": "Antonyms include tonic movements auxotonic and isotonic which are divided into concentric and eccentric."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd416188-8361-3727-8393-1edd859e7fde",
                                        "entry_id": "cf9e2bdb-0efb-317e-a45a-b9c65bdd4b8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Taking place at constant volume because of being confined by rigid boundaries."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a thermodynamic process"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
